WEBVTT

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.040
A huge-ass...

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:06.770
...hand?!

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.520
Hey, wait, just a...

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.360
Hey!

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.940
Aw, dammit!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.050
The moon!

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.710
The moon!

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:30.750
UNDERGROUND

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.490
An <i>error</i> in the Moon Cannon's firing trajectory?

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.280
You're aware of the defense mechanism on the moon's far side, correct?

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.080
Yes.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.800
Don't tell me...

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.500
Apparently their capsule encountered it.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.320
Form a search and rescue party, quickly.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.580
Yes.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.950
We're out of time.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.710
Was it trying to kill us?!

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:25.870
Sniff, sniff...

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.340
That's the smell of sunshine.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.910
So... where are we?

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.100
The planet Earthdash.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.250
The world we ought to have escaped.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.110
What?!

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.020
It feels like Hell's doorstep.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:53.160
Miss Miyuki. Miss Miyuki.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.690
Miss Miyuki!

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.250
Are you all right?

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.510
Where are we?

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.180
Apparently we fell back to the surface.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.460
Apparently we what?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:13.940
We overshot Mooneyes and were on an orbit to circle the moon when that giant hand...

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.580
Miss Miyuki, you saw those ruins too, didn't you?

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.010
And that giant?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.100
So this must be...

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:32.950
Yes.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.180
Hey, Miyuki.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.210
You okay...?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.520
A giant?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.570
Look!

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.220
What's this?!

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.940
I didn't think they could possibly be real either.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.510
The giants on the moon, huh?

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.790
I thought that was just a fairy tale.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.400
On the moon live the descendants...

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.030
...of the giants who once created the heavens.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.050
Yeah, that.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.870
My mom told me the story when I was little.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.090
And the moon giants are starfarers too...

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.080
Starfarers?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.180
Oh, that's a tasty-sounding name!

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.340
<i>Long, long, long ago,</i>

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.680
<i>the gods created the world.</i>

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.510
<i>The gods' footprints became the seas and the rivers,</i>

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:36.670
<i>and the scars of their struggle became the cornerstones of civilization.</i>

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.440
<i>It is said that the first people to play sports with a ball</i>

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.990
<i>did so in memory of that battle long ago.</i>

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.900
<i>Time passed, and a prodigious player appeared</i>

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.870
<i>whose skills rivaled the gods'.</i>

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.870
<i>That player wielded a thunderbolt ball,</i>

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.710
<i>and saved both Earthdash and the moon in their hour of need.</i>

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.300
<i>He was revered as a legend.</i>

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.740
That's pretty much how the story I know goes.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.370
A thunderbolt ball?

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.560
That ball gleamed with a radiant light,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.440
and the path it traced was the shape of the heavens' creation.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.680
Huh? What?

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.850
It's been bugging me.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.910
Why did James and his group deliberately seek us out?

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.930
Why did they make a league, and even hold championships?

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.210
For the money and... something more?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.040
Yes.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:45.970
Maybe, just maybe, the moon is searching for someone who can really hurl thunderbolt balls.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.180
And that's...

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:49.720
What's that?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.570
Hey, Iceman!

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:03.100
This is the place I least wanted to remember.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.540
I, too, was once deluded by the legend.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.600
As proof that I failed to become the man of legend,

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.560
I have this arm, and this leg.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:30.110
Now the shards of my dream lie deep within the earth.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:32.800
Iceman...

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.610
This arm <i>aches</i>.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:46.150
This leg won't be quiet.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:51.280
You...

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.120
Dan, you're not like me.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.990
You'll do it...

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.620
You'll become the true legend.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.630
Destroy!

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.140
Iceman...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.550
Dan, he still works!

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:17.140
Got it!

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.610
Wait up, Iceman!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.800
My Zephyr...

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.730
I bet I can do something.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:35.650
Leave it to me!

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.330
Please!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.410
Whew! Huh?

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:42.860
{bg}No, Jiiya, don't!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.290
How was the launch?

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:46.550
A pleasure to meet you.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.210
I am Jiiya, her companion.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.050
I figured you were being too quiet,

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.620
but you fainted even before we left, didn't you?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.840
I knew.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.390
Nice!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.940
She comes from class, doesn't she?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.310
No, no!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.060
We all have our reasons.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.390
Miss Sela...

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.820
I'll handle the repairs!

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.330
Oh... Thanks.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.990
You're not like me.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:20.240
Duh!

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.410
You and me are different!

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:22.590
Iceman!

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:29.210
Wrong side up!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.400
Ow...

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.770
What the hell?!

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:55.200
Dan!

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.260
Who are you guys?

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:03.670
Ow!

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.650
Welcome...

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.060
...to endsville. {Or shitsville. Whichever u think fits better szzzt}

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.360
Where'd you come from?

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.060
Where?

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:26.900
Don't you—?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.140
We came from up there!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.840
Where is this place?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.700
This is the abyss:

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.230
Underground.

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:34.570
Underground?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.950
Those with nowhere to go end up here.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.640
The town that is rock bottom.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.140
In this town of chaos and anarchy,

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.260
have hope and peace, for a time.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.500
Listen, all of you!

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:10.930
No! Stop! Please stop!

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.360
I don't want to die!

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.550
Stop!

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:21.740
To be chosen is both a disaster and a blessing.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:26.450
It's the first barrier you must overcome if you wish to crawl back up to the light.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:33.960
{laughs}That was quick!

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.040
Sniff, sniff.

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.360
That's the smell of blood.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.690
Let's see...

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.750
This can serve for that and the other...

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.240
And there's still...

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:51.230
This!

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.580
Let go!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.250
You let go!

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.250
I want the transforming screw from this!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.860
I want the mounting!

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:16.790
Oh!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:21.180
We'll dismantle it, give you the screw and me the mounting!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.750
Come, no time to waste!

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:23.340
Come where?!

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:26.220
You're lucky! So lucky!

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.050
H-Hey!

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.240
What are you—?!

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:34.860
Let go!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.320
Where are you taking me this time, you—?!

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.200
Hey, what—

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.390
Let me go!

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:40.670
You're lucky.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.710
Ow...

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.890
Fight, if you want to stay alive!

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.370
There are weapons over there.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.800
Wh-What?!

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:22.990
Kill him! Kill him! Kill him!

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.570
Fight!

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:25.890
There are your weapons!

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.330
If it's a weapon I need...

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.840
I pick him, of course!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.260
You moron! What are you doing?!

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.220
Pick up a weapon!

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.430
A spear or a sword or something, there's plenty!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.030
There's no points or edges I want! {sz: lit, "There's no drills or planes I want!" He seems to be talking about woodworking tools. Perhaps it's a figure for not wanting a tool with a point or an edge.}

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:55.720
Kill him! Kill him! Kill him!

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:06.650
Who did that?

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:07.860
No interference!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.710
Basquash!

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:31.050
There.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:36.980
How about...

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.440
...this?!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.700
The winner gives death to the loser!

00:12:56.700 --> 00:13:15.600
Kill him! Kill him! Kill him!

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.680
They want you to kill him.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.350
H-Hey!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:20.100
You're really gonna do it?

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:22.660
You gonna kill him? Hey!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.640
You dumbasses!

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.720
I can't basquat if I kill him!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.650
Dammit!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.230
There's no killing in basketball!

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.150
They're nuts!

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.960
It's that basketball jerk.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:31.380
That's a pretty good price.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.870
I heard they kept up the chase 'til he went to Dead Bottom.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.650
Shit! The lowest level?

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.970
Here you go.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.690
Would you fellows mind telling me more?

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:49.760
Good work.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.930
Thank you.

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.700
You're pretty popular.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.700
For a cute boy!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.400
The kinky impression is very good.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.540
Don't stare at me!

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:06.560
Yep! That's what appeals to them!

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.100
I can't believe men like this sort of thing!

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:13.400
No, no, gender has no bearing on beauty!

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.310
Artists down through the ages have all—

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.140
Jiiya!

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:18.150
Be quiet while I'm working!

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.510
Pardon me.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.640
All right everyone, we have one stage left to go!

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:26.030
No relaxing yet!

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:27.960
Okay!

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.320
Apparently Dan made it to a place called Dead Bottom.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:32.700
Bottom?

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.750
When Miyuki's done with the repairs, we'll go there too.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.450
Until then, we gather information.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:39.730
All right.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:44.250
I still can't believe it, though.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.910
Who would have thought the franchise had expanded here?

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.040
There's human industry for you.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.010
I don't mean to boast, but we have a location on the moon too.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.390
Did you find your handsome man?

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:57.890
Nope.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:15:59.950
Still...

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:03.160
It's quite something that you're a teammate of Iceman's.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.050
Yeah, well.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:08.040
He always used to drink right here at the bar.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:11.910
Said he liked the name of the place.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.820
Three in the Key...

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.110
The 3-second rule.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:21.510
And then he lost his arm and leg.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:25.370
Listen, all of you!

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:29.160
We've found you now, you basketball jerk!

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.590
Huh? He seems a little different.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.710
The only thing that matches is the basketball!

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:37.590
Wrong guy.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:44.060
My name is Iceman Hotty.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.770
Iceman Hotty?

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.660
Scream my name.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.410
And spread the word...

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:54.530
...that Iceman Hotty has returned to Underground!

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:56.610
Destroy!

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.000
Here, thanks for waiting.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.640
Thank you!

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:13.090
That's a weird screw to want, though.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.170
Is it for a Bigfoot control interface or something?

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:15.940
Huh?

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:18.470
I mean a mecha undergoing repairs. Is that for its controller or something?

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:22.850
Without a screw like that, the controls aren't loose enough to feel good, right?

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.770
Can I call you my <i>older sister</i>?!

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.140
Call me Thousand.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.990
You?

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.750
Oh, I never said.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.690
I'm Miyuki. Miyuki Ayukawa.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.410
Ayukawa...

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:38.360
What?

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:44.400
Oh, so that's it! I get it.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:47.110
Get out.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.380
Get out.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.430
Thousand?

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:53.900
I hate you.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:54.880
Just get out!

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:07.250
Dan!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.560
There's a road on the other side.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.300
A tasty, tasty smell is calling me.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.580
Excellent!

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:16.570
I doubt they'll chase us all the way down here.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.360
It's pretty amazing we got down here.

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:23.250
That's Basquash.

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:25.740
Only someone basquatting could come down that slope.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:29.950
That looks like a slope to you?

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:39.020
Oh yeah, why are we in this mess again?

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:40.130
Like I know!

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:44.220
Anyways, the best we can do is get outside and meet up with Miyuki and the rest...

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.640
Now this is unusual.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.990
I heard lately you're some big shot on the surface,

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.010
General Manager Yan.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:14.160
A boy fell here from the surface.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.130
You want me to kill him?

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:20.210
If he's really the man of legend, I doubt he'll die.

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:23.880
Legend? Oh, I can kill legends.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:28.280
You know him?

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:31.100
He's a lucky boy.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.950
He was last seen heading toward Dead Bottom from the underground river.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.590
Can you get there?

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:38.900
Who do you think I am?

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:41.750
I'm Price.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.450
I'm the price of Hell.

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:56.850
Dan! Hey, wake up, Dan!

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.750
Man, you're loud...

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.450
One of your relatives?

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:10.870
I don't believe in cannibalism.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:23.750
A ball?

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:24.780
Look at that!

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.220
Who's that?

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.080
What're you gonna do?

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:40.250
Right now I've got a ball!

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:45.050
I'm the Basquasher, Dan JD!

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.310
What on Earth are Dan and Iceman up to?

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:59.100
They're both excellent Basquashers. They'll be fine.

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:01.440
I really have no luck with men.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.730
Next time: Giant Step.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:07.730
NEXT TIME

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:03.020
GIANT STEP

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:07.730
GIANT STEP

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:06.120
I foresee a new encounter!

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.240
Really?!
